<div class="terminal" aria-label="Example CAO setup commands followed by a campaign installation request to an agent">
  <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
    <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
    <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
    <span class="terminal-title">CAO — setup + agent request</span>
  </div>
  <div class="terminal-body">
    <div class="terminal-label">In an existing control repository checkout</div>
    <div class="terminal-line command" style="--line-delay: 0ms">
      <span class="prompt">$</span>
      <code><span class="syntax-command">gh</span> extension install githubnext/gh-cao</code>
    </div>
    <pre class="terminal-output" data-terminal-output="install">Installed extension githubnext/gh-cao</pre>
    <div class="terminal-line command" style="--line-delay: 550ms">
      <span class="prompt">$</span>
      <code><span class="syntax-command">gh cao</span> setup</code>
    </div>
    <pre class="terminal-output" data-terminal-output="setup">Monitoring configured locally. No commit or push was performed.
Next: gh cao doctor, then review, commit and push the installed files.
Optional automation: https://githubnext.github.io/gh-cao/operation-patterns/</pre>
    <div class="terminal-label">Setup can separately offer reviewed publication; declining leaves files local.</div>
    <div class="terminal-label">Example agent request — not a CLI command</div>
    <div class="terminal-line command" style="--line-delay: 1100ms">
      <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
      <code>Add the Dependabot campaign to CAO<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></code>
    </div>
    <pre class="terminal-output" data-terminal-request="integration">Install githubnext/gh-cao/dependabot.
Use its central orchestrator and one-target workers.
Keep policy disabled, review-only, and scoped to one repo.
Review the campaign files and policy. Do not enable or run.</pre>
  </div>
</div>

